@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Form Filling - Demo Page";
}

<div id="content">
    <!--  CONTENT   -->
    <div id="page-header" class="page-demo">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="span12 whitebg">
                <h1>Demo <span>Form Filling</span></h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">


        <div class="span12">

            <p>
                In a few seconds SeeShell 
                <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf4eJ125g4G6AzS1rJwoPADlfADnfv4fvuKfmOf1NZXohlB2A/viewform?hl=en">will click this link</a>,
                which will bring you to a regular  <span class="hired">multi-page</span>Google form,
                with plenty of Javascript and CSS. Once there, the SeeShell Browser
                fills out the forms and submits it.
            <p> The goal of this demo is to show that SeeShell is ideal for filling out multi-page forms, and it shows the use of the CLICK and CLICKTYPE commands.</p>
 

            <p>The form is also used by the  Demo-ManyPlay-Part1/2/3 macros, which are used by the PowerShell 
                <a href="/seeshell/api">SeeShell Scripting API</a> demo. You find the corresponding Powershell file in the /SeeShell.Browser/API folder 
            or on <a href="https://github.com/A9T9/SeeShell/">Github</a>.
             The show how to concatenate several <a href="https://ui.vision/seeshell/docs#play">Play API</a> calls.</p>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
